# Lockfiles ARE committed, both of them, and deliberately.
#
# Cargo.lock is committed even though this workspace publishes libraries, where
# the older convention was to omit it. This project pins wgpu exactly (HLD
# 15.2) because agents emit APIs from the wrong era, and section 36 wants
# reproducible output across three targets. A floating transitive dependency
# would undo both. package-lock.json is committed because CI runs `npm ci`,
# which refuses to run without it.

# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# proptest writes a seed file next to a failing property test so the
# failure can be replayed. Useful locally, and noise in a diff: the
# ones that appear during a review's mutation runs record deliberately
# broken code.
**/*.proptest-regressions

# Python bytecode from the guard scripts. Appears the moment one is imported
# as a module rather than run as a script.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# wasm-pack output. Built by bin/ocelli.sh wasm, never committed.
crates/ocelli-wasm/pkg/
crates/ocelli-wasm/target/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/

# The corpus. See corpus/README.md. The manifest IS committed, the data is not.
corpus/data/
*.dcm
*.dicom
*.DCM

# Oracle output: rendered frames, diffs, hashes for one run.
tools/oracle/out/
tools/oracle/node_modules/
.playwright/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Verification ledger is per-clone evidence, not shared history.
.claude/verify-ledger.json

# In-flight agent notes. Everything else under .claude/ IS committed:
# plans, reviews, commands and handoffs are tracked, agent-neutral artefacts.
.claude/scratch/

# Local settings override
.claude/settings.local.json

# Credentials. Nothing here should ever exist in this repository, and the
# patterns are cheap insurance rather than a substitute for not creating them.
# A crates.io or npm token lives in CI secrets, never on disk.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
.npmrc
.cargo/credentials
.cargo/credentials.toml

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
.playwright-mcp/

# Where the private source documents live on THIS machine. Per-clone, because
# it is a property of the checkout and not of the project.
.ocelli-source-path
